== 1.8 Chapter 1 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The first of the six moves is to ask],
  [which option is longest],
  [which theme the passage illustrates],
  [which text, genre and writer the stem belongs to],
  [which character is speaking]
)

#mcq(2, [A set-text question almost always contains],
  [two quotations and a name],
  [a location and a judgment],
  [a date and a summary],
  [a quotation and a definition]
)

#mcq(3, [Which move eliminates an option that describes the right event at the wrong point in the text?],
  [Check],
  [Effect],
  [Place],
  [Locate]
)

#mcq(4, [The sixth move, check, exists to catch],
  [a true statement that answers a different question],
  [a quotation from another text],
  [a misspelt character name],
  [an option longer than the others]
)

#mcq(5, [Set-text distractors are dangerous because they are],
  [always about minor characters],
  [built from real features of the text],
  [obviously false],
  [usually longer than the key]
)

#mcq(6, [A fact question about a set text should cost roughly],
  [two minutes],
  [five minutes],
  [ten seconds],
  [forty seconds]
)

#mcq(7, [A scene question asks you to supply],
  [the theme of the whole text],
  [the date of publication],
  [the position of the line and who is present],
  [the writer's biography]
)

#mcq(8, [A question on technique asks for the device and],
  [its Latin name],
  [the number of times it appears],
  [the writer's other works],
  [what it does in the plot or for the audience]
)

#mcq(9, [An option that offers only an adjective, such as she is kind, is usually wrong because],
  [it describes the writer rather than the character],
  [it gives a judgment without the scene that proves it],
  [it is too short to be an answer],
  [adjectives are never used in the paper]
)

#mcq(10, [When a who-says-this stem could fit two characters, the stem will contain],
  [a quotation from the title],
  [a detail that only one of them could know],
  [a reference to the writer],
  [the name of the act]
)

#mcq(11, [A biography option is a distractor unless the stem],
  [uses the word theme],
  [asks about a character],
  [names the writer],
  [quotes a line]
)

#mcq(12, [The three lines of a scene card are who wanted what, what it cost, and],
  [the theme it proves],
  [who else was present],
  [the line you would quote],
  [the chapter number]
)

#mcq(13, [A play can be reduced to about twenty-five scene cards and a novel to about],
  [thirty],
  [sixty],
  [ten],
  [a hundred]
)

#mcq(14, [Copying another candidate's scene cards is useless because],
  [their handwriting is different],
  [writing the card is itself the revision],
  [the paper does not test quotations],
  [the cards are always wrong]
)

#mcq(15, [In an answer, a quotation should function as],
  [evidence],
  [a way of lengthening the option],
  [a substitute for the scene],
  [decoration]
)

#mcq(16, [When a stem quotes half a line, the first task is to],
  [name the device],
  [identify the play],
  [count the feet],
  [complete the context]
)

#mcq(17, [The commonest order of failure in the exam hall is],
  [reading the options before locating the scene],
  [skipping a hard question],
  [reading the stem twice],
  [checking the clock]
)

#mcq(18, [Answering from a film adaptation is unsafe because adaptations change],
  [scene order and who is present],
  [the price of the book],
  [the number of acts only],
  [the writer's name]
)

#mcq(19, [Of the five prescribed texts in this volume, the two that are drama are],
